Review written to `docs/reviews/equipment-hvac/equip-hvac-03-hp-defrost-cycle-tracker.md` — 4 findings:

| Severity | Finding |
|----------|---------|
| **High** | No frost decay during extended off-periods; first call after shoulder season triggers spurious defrost (`defrost.rs:269-283`). OCHRE avoids this by having no persistent accumulator state. |
| **Medium** | Step-local `interval_s` computation uses instantaneous rather than averaged `time_fraction`, breaking long-run defrost fraction when OAT oscillates (`defrost.rs:278`). |
| **Medium** | No hysteresis on `evaluate_defrost` activation threshold; rapid toggle at 4.4445°C boundary (`defrost.rs:369-374`). Parity with OCHRE but both share the deficiency. |
| **Low** | Defrosting timer progresses when compressor is off, causing state/physics mismatch after interrupted defrost cycles (`defrost.rs:285-293`). |
